      "body": "### Apache-2.0 license compliance issue regarding derived vcmi-gym code\n\nThe repository \"c18593395/vcmi-strategic-gym\" contains source code derived from  [smanolloff/vcmi-gym](https://github.com/smanolloff/vcmi-gym), including files that retain my copyright notice and Apache-2.0 license header. vcmi-gym is distributed under the Apache License 2.0.\n\nYour repository currently describes itself as MIT-licensed and contains an MIT LICENSE, but does not appear to include a copy of the Apache License 2.0 as required by §4(a) for redistribution of Apache-licensed material.\n\nAdditionally, Apache-2.0 §4(b) requires modified files to carry prominent notices stating that they have been changed.\n\nPlease bring the repository into compliance by preserving the Apache-2.0 licensing requirements applicable to the incorporated vcmi-gym code, including the required license and notices, clearly identifying the origin of those portions, and marking modified Apache-derived files accordingly.\n\nThe vcmi-strategic-gym repository contains substantial code derived from vcmi-gym, but does not present itself as a fork or otherwise identify vcmi-gym as its source. It currently has a short independent commit history and describes itself as a separate project named “VCMI Strategic Gym.”\n\nThe \"c18593395/vcmi-strategic-gym\" repository's README states:\n\n“MIT (this repository). VCMI engine code is GPL-2.0+.”\n\nIts top-level LICENSE is MIT and states:\n\n“Copyright (c) 2026 cmi-strategic-gym contributors”\n\nAt present, there does not appear to be a repository-level copy of the Apache-2.0 license covering the incorporated vcmi-gym code.\n\nGiven the substantial amount of Apache-licensed code from [smanolloff/vcmi-gym](https://github.com/smanolloff/vcmi-gym) incorporated into the \"c18593395/vcmi-strategic-gym\" repository, the current licensing and attribution appear inconsistent with the requirements of Apache License 2.0. Please take prompt action to bring the repository into compliance.",
